/* Simplified Chinese.

   The key is the English text exactly as it is written in the code; an
   interpolated value appears in the key as %@ (or %lld for an integer in a
   SwiftUI literal), so Text("Hello \(name)") is looked up as "Hello %@".
   A translation that reorders or drops a value numbers them: %1, %2.

   Wording follows the Android app's values-zh/strings.xml wherever the same
   thing already has a name there. Strings with no entry stay English on
   purpose: system-log lines, protocol names, technical error text. */


